WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:08.680
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and for my latest
bonus video I wanted to travel in to the past

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.130
and talk about the Bloodraven.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.860
He’s featured on the show but since they
cut so much stuff out about characters backstories

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:19.751
I’m making this to just shine a light on
all the awesome stuff we’re not going to

00:00:19.751 --> 00:00:27.070
get to see.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:30.580
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m doing bonus videos each week to supplement

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.580
stuff the show is skipping or just not explaining
very well.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.780
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
leave me suggestions for future bonus videos.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.780
My episode reviews usually post right after
new episodes air.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.780
I’m even doing a special giveaway.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.160
Also, if you want to talk about show stuff
that hasn’t happened yet please add a spoiler

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.160
tag at the beginning of your comment.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.160
So let’s get started.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.260
The Bloodraven is the nickname given to Brynden
Rivers.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.120
So I’m going to actually call him by his
Rivers name for most of this video.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.839
Most of the early part of his life revolved
around the Blackfyre rebellion.

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:53.780
That was the great war started when Aegon
Targaryen the fourth legitimized all his bastards

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.479
and gave one of them the famous Targaryen
sword also named Blackfyre and the lawful

00:00:58.479 --> 00:01:08.860
heirs flipped out and civil war erupted.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.980
The other famous Targaryen Valyrian sword
that used to belong to Aegon’s older sister

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.600
Visenya was given to Brynden.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.860
It’s name was Dark Sister.

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.420
One of those bastards that survived went on
to found the Golden Company, remember in episode

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.860
3 how Ser Davos talked about maybe using them.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.660
That’s going to be a whole different bonus
video I’ll do.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:33.060
It gives you an idea of just how people in
the story are connected across time and space.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.060
Just like Brynden Rivers the bloodraven.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:39.470
He lived for a long long time, so his history
is also the history of a lot of westeros before

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.910
the events on the show started.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:46.840
He’s most notable for his appearance and
his ability to use magic.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:55.000
Most of his peers called him a sorcerer, like
Ser Davos might think of Melisandre as a witch.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.380
But his powers included glamouring, skinchanging
and greensight.

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:05.850
Glamouring is similar to what you see Jaquen
H’gar do when he changes his face, but because

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.249
we don’t know how he did that I’m going
to say that what Jaquen and the Faceless Ones

00:02:10.249 --> 00:02:13.610
do to change their appearance is different
from glamouring.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:16.670
But essentially they both involve changing
your face.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.359
Skinchanging we’ve all seen on the show
and we even got a good first person shot of

00:02:20.359 --> 00:02:24.889
Bran inside Summer while he was stalking prey.

00:02:24.889 --> 00:02:28.670
Greensight is mostly referred to as the ability
to have visions of the future.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.140
Like being a prophet.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:35.499
Some magic you can learn, but greensight is
something you have to be born with.

00:02:35.499 --> 00:02:40.689
And like one person in a hundred thousand
is born with the ability.

00:02:40.689 --> 00:02:42.120
So it’s super rare.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.249
So you can understand why a lot of people
thought Brynden Rivers was an evil sorcerer.

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:55.279
But on top of that, when he was young, he
also got a lot of hate for getting Visenya’s

00:02:55.279 --> 00:02:57.719
ancenstral blade Dark Sister.

00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:01.650
Remember how much of a big deal it was when
Tywin melted down Ned Starks Valyrian blade

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.329
and gave one to Jaime and one to Joffrey.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:08.629
Everyone is jealous of someone who possesses
a Valyrian Blade.

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:14.330
When the Blackfyre Rebellion ended he sat
on the king’s small council, who was his

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.330
half brother.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:19.989
He sided with the Targaryen loyalists during
the rebellion.

00:03:19.989 --> 00:03:22.139
Eventually he became master of whispers.

00:03:22.139 --> 00:03:24.540
That’s what Varys is right now.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.480
It’s a lot like being a spymaster.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.430
That’s what Varys is talking about every
time he says “a little bird told me something

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:33.430
something…”

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:38.090
You can see why people didn’t trust Brynden,
no one trusts Varys.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:41.109
And he doesn’t have magical abilities like
Brynden had.

00:03:41.109 --> 00:03:45.541
He went on to become Hand of the King, but
one of the new Kings hated him so much he

00:03:45.541 --> 00:03:53.900
threw him in the black cells underneath the
Red Keep.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.930
It’s basically where the king throws people
when he wants to forget about them.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:04.359
If you remember Maester Aemon told Jon Snow
about how he joined the Night’s Watch, he

00:04:04.359 --> 00:04:12.620
was the brother of King Aegon the fifth.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:22.300
He was originally supposed to be king but
that’s a giant story for a whole other bonus

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.300
video.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.000
Whenever Maester Aemon went to the Night’s
Watch, Brynden Rivers was taken out of the

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.080
Black Cells and sent to the Wall with him.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.150
Brynden was much older than Maester Aemon
became Lord Commander.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.670
And eventually people just forgot about him,
which is where the events of the show pick

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.670
up.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:44.050
So hopefully episode 4 will explain what the
show is going to do with the character.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.040
They change a lot of things, so we’ll have
to wait and see.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.720
What I’m really hoping is that George RR
Martin’s new book World of Ice and Fire

00:04:50.720 --> 00:05:00.980
will fill in some of the gaps that the regular
novels and the show won’t cover.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:08.360
One of the things that makes all this so much
fun to talk about is that there’s so much

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.670
history that you could spend all your time
on it.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:16.670
The Bloodraven is the hand of the king when
the stuff in the Dunk and Egg stories are

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:17.670
happening.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.030
But he’s not really featured in those stories.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:23.320
There’s also this really cool book that
Martin has teased called Fire and Blood and

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:26.790
it’s the entire history of the Targaryen
family from Valyria to Daenerys.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:31.690
He’s not going to write that until he’s
done with the last Ice and Fire book, so that

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:44.710
will fill in a lot of the gaps too.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:48.380
The show hasn’t really just started to touch
on the gods Melisandre has been talking about,

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.570
the great other and the red god.

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.810
I’m really interested to see how the addition
of the greenseers and the children of the

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.820
forest get tied up in it all.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:04.030
I want to think of nature as being like a
neutral force between the two major gods.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.870
But it almost gets too complicated when you
start thinking about how all the supernatural

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.600
forces interact on the show.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:12.440
That’s the way I think of the Bloodraven,
as like this third thing going on off to the

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:16.340
side while you have white walkers and Melisandre
focusing on their war.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:24.130
Like I said, the Bloodraven has watched so
much of history that he kind of passes through

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.770
everyone elses story across time, whether
they know it or not.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.950
I think one of my other future bonus videos
will have to cover the Children of the Forest,

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.060
just because they also have greensight and
that’s really where things pick up on the

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.060
show.

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:38.090
I’ll probably wait till we see that play
out, just because even the books haven’t

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.490
covered a lot of their history.

00:06:39.490 --> 00:06:46.090
One of the most fun things about doing research
for all this is that you end up having to

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.980
do research on a ton of other things because
everything is connected.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:53.490
Aegon’s Conquest all the way to where the
show is right now.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:58.330
I guess that’s just a testament to good
story planning on George RR Martin’s part.

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.590
But let me know what you’re looking forward
to learning about most either on the show

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:02.590
or in the new books.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:06.210
My next bonus video will probably be explaining
all the tribes of the wildlings and how the

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:07.580
show is dealing with them.

